\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset

 Although ChemGen supplies a direct solver,
 to address the 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{O}\left(n^{3}\right)$
\end_inset

 cost,
 its default linear solver is the Generalized Minimal Residual (GMRES) method
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "Saa86"
literal "false"

\end_inset

,
 which is implemented as a standalone function.
 GMRES is an iterative Krylov subspace method that builds an orthonormal basis of the Krylov subspace and minimizes the residual over this subspace at each iteration.
 
\begin_inset Note Note
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The order of operations needed for GMRES is 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{O}\left(kn_{s}^{2}+k^{2}n_{s}+k^{3}\right)$
\end_inset

 where 
\begin_inset Formula $k$
\end_inset

 is the number of iterations required to converge.
 For well conditioned matrix the 
\begin_inset Formula $n_{s}^{2}$
\end_inset

 term can dominate thus reducing the overall cost of the linear solve.
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

